WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.430
February 2019 will see a ton of new Netflix
content, with exciting new releases in every

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.500
major genre.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.950
We've rounded up the best of the best to showcase
everything great coming to Netflix in February

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:11.950
2019.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:16.661
Natasha Lyonne of Orange Is the New Black
produced and stars in Russian Doll, a series

00:00:16.661 --> 00:00:21.339
about a woman forced to relive the night of
a big party over and over again, an experience

00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:23.659
which is always rudely interrupted by her
death.

00:00:23.659 --> 00:00:27.539
Forget the obvious similarity to Happy Death
Day; the always-entertaining Lyonne told The

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:28.539
Hollywood Reporter

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:31.460
"It's an autobiography wrapped in a mind-bending
concept.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.350
I'm 100 percent in there and most definitely
the architect of the whole thing."

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.309
This show not only sports a deadpan sense
of humor, but has the potential to get very

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:44.059
interesting very quickly, and the first season
drops on February 1st.

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:48.739
The third feature from Nightcrawler director
Dan Gilroy reunites him with that amazing

00:00:48.739 --> 00:00:53.270
film's lead actors Jake Gyllenhaal and Rene
Russo, along with John Malkovich and Toni

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:54.270
Collette.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.149
It's the story of a Soho art gallery owner
and a vicious critic who come into possession

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:02.249
of the works of an artist whose recent death
is shrouded in mystery… and they soon wish

00:01:02.249 --> 00:01:03.980
they hadn't.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.340
"It's connected to his art!"

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:15.500
The flick's insane trailer promises a mind-bending
ride, a committed performance from Gyllenhaal,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.190
and a bunch of profoundly creepy imagery.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.470
This is Gilroy's first foray into flat-out
horror, and you can give it a watch on February

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.470
1st.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:27.500
The Finnish detective series Bordertown was
picked up for international distribution by

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.340
Netflix after its debut season, which went
on to strike a chord with streaming audiences

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.700
with its dark, compelling storytelling.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:38.770
Fans of shows like The Killing and True Detective
will find Bordertown to be a treat; when the

00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:43.110
first episode of season 1 aired on Finnish
television, it was watched by over a million

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:44.110
viewers.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.250
If you haven't checked out the first batch
of episodes, you may want to catch up before

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.210
season 2 drops on February 2nd.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.841
Screenwriter Tarell Alvin McCraney picked
up an Oscar for co-scripting the 2016 Best

00:01:54.841 --> 00:01:55.841
Picture winner Moonlight.

00:01:55.841 --> 00:02:00.590
For his next trick, he's giving us High Flying
Bird, a fictionalized account of the efforts

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.670
of a sports agent to salvage the careers of
his clients in the wake of the real-life 2011

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:05.670
NBA lockout.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:10.610
Oh, and in the director's chair is Steven
Soderbergh, whose recent successes include

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.820
Logan Lucky and the psychological thriller
Unsane.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:18.090
The sports drama is scoring big time with
critics; you can give it a shot when it premieres

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.870
on February 8th.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:23.680
The Break is a Belgian series which follows
the attempt of a veteran police detective

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.960
to escape from his demons by returning to
his peaceful, relatively murder-free hometown.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.170
But things take a turn for the worse when
a body is discovered, leading our protagonist

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.350
down a sinister path.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:37.920
The first season was well-received by critics
who appreciated its bleak cinematography and

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.280
snappy, well-written dialogue; the noir-ish
drama makes its return with season 2 on February

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.280
9th.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.850
Daily Show veteran Hasan Minaj made a splash
with the first season of his insightful political

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:53.920
comedy series Patriot Act, in which he explores
topics relevant to today's society through

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.530
the filter of his unique comedic sensibility.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.120
Each episode focuses on a single topic, which
Minhaj delves into through a combination of

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.910
standup, interviews, and on location segments.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.010
Minhaj's cutting yet thoughtful brand of political
humor is perhaps something we can all use

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:12.040
more of right now, and season 2 of Patriot
Act will give us just that when it drops on

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.420
February 10th.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:19.050
The Breaker Upperers is a comedy film from
New Zealand with Thor: Ragnarok director involved

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.560
as an executive producer.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.310
"Look at this world, amazement!

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:27.310
What’s through this door?

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.819
Oh Australia."

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:33.130
Sami and Jackie van Beek, directors of The
Breaker Upperers, came into Waititi's orbit

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:37.569
when they appeared as actors in his features
What We Do in the Shadows and Eagle versus

00:03:37.569 --> 00:03:38.569
Shark.

00:03:38.569 --> 00:03:42.490
In addition to directing, the pair also star
as cynical friends who go into business breaking

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.800
up couples for profit.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.140
"I'm sorry Jeff, it's over"

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.810
"What?"

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:57.340
The film scored with critics when it made
the festival rounds, and it'll likely score

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.780
with you when it hits the small screen on
February 15th.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:05.569
Based on a Dark Horse comic book series created
by Gerard Way, the original series The Umbrella

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:10.440
Academy follows a group of children with otherworldly
powers who were all born simultaneously on

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.390
the same day in 1989.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:16.620
Brought together in their teen years by a
mysterious billionaire, they all regroup 17

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.219
years later upon their benefactor's death
in an attempt to get to the bottom of the

00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:21.949
events surrounding his passing.

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:26.809
Get ready for superpowered intrigue when the
first season drops on February 15th.

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:31.840
This violent period piece from Korea explores
the rise of a petty crook from Busan who ups

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.800
his game by diving into the Asian narcotics
trade of the 1970's.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:40.229
Eventually, he becomes - you guessed it - a
drug king, struggling to hold his place atop

00:04:40.229 --> 00:04:44.629
his organization while pouring a steady stream
of contraband into Japan and keeping up a

00:04:44.629 --> 00:04:46.900
front as a benevolent community leader.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.510
Look for it on February 21.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:54.559
Paddleton is the sophomore feature from director
Alex Lehmann, and stars co-writer Mark Duplass

00:04:54.559 --> 00:04:58.960
alongside Ray Romano as odd couple neighbors
who develop an unlikely friendship.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.949
Their bond is quickly put to the test, however,
when one of them receives a terminal cancer

00:05:02.949 --> 00:05:03.949
diagnosis.

00:05:03.949 --> 00:05:08.039
The flick absolutely wowed critics on the
festival circuit, with Romano's performance

00:05:08.039 --> 00:05:10.439
in particular being singled out for praise.

00:05:10.439 --> 00:05:13.319
"What's the worst case scenario we run out
of gas?"

00:05:13.319 --> 00:05:15.659
"Worst case scenario is we run out of gas
right here and next thing you know, we’re

00:05:15.659 --> 00:05:16.659
drinking our urine."

00:05:16.659 --> 00:05:20.080
You'll definitely want to check out Paddleton
when it makes its streaming debut on February

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.689
22.

00:05:21.689 --> 00:05:25.599
There's more than meets the eye to the French
drama Paris is Us, the story of a young woman

00:05:25.599 --> 00:05:27.120
who returns to her home city.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.270
The trailer promises a blurring of the lines
between fantasy and reality, as our heroine

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:36.259
begins to draw parallels between her traumatic
recent past and events in the world at large.

00:05:36.259 --> 00:05:41.150
"It's now that everything is possible, even
if this life may be just a dream."

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:47.100
The Kickstarter funded project was shot between
2014 and 2017 before being picked up by Netflix.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:51.139
Paris has not been resting easy as of late,
and this incorporates some real-world tension

00:05:51.139 --> 00:05:52.990
into its rather trippy narrative.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:55.949
You can check it out on February 22nd.

00:05:55.949 --> 00:06:00.719
Suburra is a gritty Italian crime series centered
on a seaside town near Rome, which various

00:06:00.719 --> 00:06:04.150
interested parties have designs on turning
into a gambling resort.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:07.979
Coming into conflict with each other over
these plans are a prominent Roman family,

00:06:07.979 --> 00:06:11.589
a slew of corrupt politicians, the Catholic
church, and the Mafia.

00:06:11.589 --> 00:06:16.229
The series' first season drew favorable comparisons
with The Wire, and was widely praised for

00:06:16.229 --> 00:06:18.509
its stark tone and thriller-esque pacing.

00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:22.619
Profane, raw, and violent, it's been called
"the kind of show that grabs your attention

00:06:22.619 --> 00:06:25.319
and doesn't let go" - perfect for binge-watching.

00:06:25.319 --> 00:06:26.820
Season 2 premieres on February 22.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:27.820
Those are all the best Netflix originals showing
up in February, but there's plenty more to

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:28.820
look forward to!

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:33.210
There are a few choice selections for thriller
fans in February, most notably the first installment

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.589
of the long-running Final Destination series.

00:06:35.589 --> 00:06:40.249
That arrives with the entirety of the Jaws
franchise, from Steven Spielberg's benchmark-setting

00:06:40.249 --> 00:06:45.139
original to Jaws: The Revenge, a feature that
regularly winds up in discussion of the worst

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:46.389
films of all time.

00:06:46.389 --> 00:06:52.050
"Damn passengers are all the same, complain
complain.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.469
Oh snap!"

00:06:53.469 --> 00:06:57.189
Those show up on the first, alongside a number
of beloved comedies.

00:06:57.189 --> 00:07:01.180
Starting this month, look for the warm Hugh
Grant vehicle About a Boy and the first three

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:02.740
American Pie movies.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:06.949
Later in the month, Steve Carell's breakout
film The 40-Year Old Virgin arrives on the

00:07:06.949 --> 00:07:12.279
16th, followed by the comedy-drama Our Idiot
Brother on the 26th.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.219
"Come in."

00:07:17.219 --> 00:07:20.800
Only a pair of new drama offerings are making
their way to Netflix this month, but they're

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.819
both well worth a watch.

00:07:22.819 --> 00:07:28.220
2016's The Edge of Seventeen features burgeoning
star Hailee Steinfeld in a thoughtful coming-of-age

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.240
drama and drops on the first.

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:35.409
And on the sixth, look for 2009's The Soloist
starring Robert Downey, Jr. as a newspaper

00:07:35.409 --> 00:07:40.379
columnist who becomes unlikely friends with
a blind violinist played by Jamie Foxx.

00:07:40.379 --> 00:07:44.969
Finally, Netflix is premiering three new original
comedy specials in February.

00:07:44.969 --> 00:07:50.120
On the fifth, Ray Romano returns to New York's
famed Comedy Cellar after 23 years to deliver

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.969
a new standup set in Right Here, Around the
Corner.

00:07:52.969 --> 00:07:57.529
Kevin Hart examines the contributions of African
Americans through his uniquely cracked lens

00:07:57.529 --> 00:07:59.259
in a new special available on the 8th.

00:07:59.259 --> 00:08:03.819
And the hilarious Ken Jeong delivers a Valentine's
Day set of silliness in his first Netflix

00:08:03.819 --> 00:08:05.039
special on the 14th.

00:08:05.039 --> 00:08:06.460
"You can't do that."

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.219
"Have you met me?"

00:08:08.219 --> 00:08:10.139
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:08:10.139 --> 00:08:13.710
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:17.389
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

